-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_44.sql (Isaiah 44) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 44 — Yahuah the Maker and Former vs. the man who fashions a dead block; the Spirit
-- poured on the seed; the First and the Last beside whom there is no Elohim; pardon unto return; Cyrus
-- named. *Thus saith Yahuah (LORD) that made thee, and formed thee from the womb* (44:2) frames the whole:
-- Yahuah FORMS his people and the heavens (44:24), the idolater only FASHIONS (44:9-19) — the Former
-- versus the formed-by-hands.
-- Tag: isa44   Temp view: _s303_isa44_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27075, step 3 -> threads at 27075, 27078, 27081, 27084, 27087 (5 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',44,v
--
-- ⚠ 44:20 BINDING: a PRE-EXISTING thread (slug 'counterfeit-right-hand...', NOT an isaiah-44- slug)
--   already carries the 44:20 "deceived heart / a lie in his right hand" idol-self-deception punchline.
--   I CENTER my idol thread on 44:9-19 (the carpenter/smith making the god) and do NOT mint a thread on
--   44:20. I cite 44:20 ONLY in passing prose to bound the unit; no member row anchors at 44:20; no
--   thematic duplicate of the deceived-heart/lie-in-the-right-hand idea. No slug collision (mine all
--   start isaiah-44-).
